**How to set it up:**

1. **Install CrookCatcher** from <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.harteg.crookcatcher&referrer=utm_source%3Dwebsite%26utm_medium%3Dguide%26utm_campaign%3Dlock-screen-message-android" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Play</a> and finish the setup. Taking the photo and emailing it are free.
2. **Turn on Show message** in the app's settings for failed unlocks. Show message is part of CrookCatcher Pro.
3. **Open the editor.** Write your text, then choose a background color, **Your picture** or **Crook's photo**.
4. **Tap "See it full screen"** to check how it looks.
5. **Test it.** Lock your phone and enter a wrong PIN.

The message closes when the person presses back or the screen turns off, and the phone stays locked the whole time.

Use both kinds of message together: Android's permanent text for the honest finder, and Show message for everyone else.

<AppCta position="guide_mid" />

## What to write on the screen

- **For a lost phone:** "This phone is lost. Please call 555 0100. Reward." A way to reach you matters more than anything else.
- **For a thief:** short and factual works better than angry. "Your photo and this location were just sent to the owner."
- **For family and friends:** this is where the meme goes.

Don't threaten anyone, and don't go to meet a thief yourself. Give the photo and the location to the police.

## Frequently Asked Questions

### Q: How do I put my contact info on my Android lock screen?
A: Go to `Settings > Display > Lock screen > Add text on lock screen`. On a Samsung Galaxy, go to `Settings > Lock screen and AOD > Contact information`.

### Q: Can I put a message on a phone I've already lost?
A: Yes, if it's switched on and online. Open Find Hub at google.com/android/find, choose the phone and tap **Mark as lost**. You can enter contact information and a message for the lock screen.

### Q: Can I show a picture on the lock screen when someone enters the wrong PIN?
A: Not with Android's own settings. CrookCatcher's Show message does this: after a wrong PIN, pattern or password it shows a full-screen picture with your text.

### Q: Can my phone show a thief their own photo?
A: Yes. In CrookCatcher's Show message editor, choose **Crook's photo** as the background. The photo taken at the wrong unlock attempt is shown on the screen with your text on top.

### Q: Is Show message free?
A: Show message is a CrookCatcher Pro feature. The free version takes the photo and emails it to you with the location.

### Q: Does the message unlock the phone or give the person access?
A: No. The message is shown on top of the lock screen. The phone stays locked, and the person still needs your PIN, pattern or password.

